<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:spiffworkflow="http://spiffworkflow.org/bpmn/schema/1.0/core" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="Definitions_ThreatSourceDiscovery" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn">
  <bpmn:process id="threat_source_discovery_process" name="Threat Source Discovery" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:documentation>Daily scan for new threat-monitoring sources and keywords (WI-002203). Replaces onefm_mcp's LangGraph "Agent 1" (threat_sources_expansion_agent): load the active keyword list and the existing approved sources, ask the Threat Source Expander agent for new candidate sources, drop duplicate suggestions, ask the Threat Keyword Generator agent for new keywords, then write everything to Threat Source (Pending) and Threat Keyword (AI Generated). No human step — this is a pure background batch pipeline, so there is a single unnamed lane.

Two things the original LangGraph pipeline did are deliberately dropped, not ported: HTTP liveness-checking existing sources, and re-checking each AI-suggested URL's reachability before accepting it. BPMN-linked Server Scripts are AST-gated (one_bpmn.security.script_gate) and permanently forbid `requests`/`urllib` — any outbound HTTP has to go through the declarative Connector system instead, and connectors dispatch one call per Service Task, not a loop over a variable-length list. Wiring that would need a Multi-Instance Service Task per URL, which is real added complexity for a check whose only original consumer was the Pending-review dashboard — every source this pipeline creates already lands as status=Pending and needs human approval before Feed Collection ever reads it, so an unreachable URL is caught at review time instead of pipeline time.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="timer_start" name="Daily Schedule">
      <bpmn:outgoing>f1</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:timerEventDefinition id="TimerEventDefinition_Daily">
        <bpmn:timeCycle xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">0 9 * * *</bpmn:timeCycle>
      </bpmn:timerEventDefinition>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="load_keywords" name="Load Active Keywords" spiffworkflow:serverScript="Threat Discovery — Load Active Keywords" spiffworkflow:scriptType="Server Script" spiffworkflow:scriptName="Threat Discovery — Load Active Keywords">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads every Threat Keyword with is_active=1 into active_keywords.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>f1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="load_existing_sources" name="Load Existing Approved Sources" spiffworkflow:serverScript="Threat Discovery — Load Existing Approved Sources" spiffworkflow:scriptType="Server Script" spiffworkflow:scriptName="Threat Discovery — Load Existing Approved Sources">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads every Threat Source with status=Approved into existing_sources, used as the AI step's context of what already exists. No HTTP liveness check here — see the process-level documentation on why that step was dropped rather than ported.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>f2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="expand_sources" name="AI Agent Task: Expand Source List" spiffworkflow:serviceType="ai_agent" spiffworkflow:aiAgentConfig="Threat Source Expander" spiffworkflow:aiStopOnError="false" spiffworkflow:aiOutputVariable="expansion_result" spiffworkflow:aiResponseFormat="json" spiffworkflow:aiUserPrompt="Current approved threat monitoring sources ({{ existing_sources | length }} total, showing up to 15):&#10;&#10;{% for s in (existing_sources or [])[:15] %}- {{ s.source_name }} ({{ s.source_type }}): {{ s.source_url }}&#10;{% endfor %}&#10;Suggest 5 NEW and real sources (websites, news pages, or social media channels) relevant to security, crime or public-safety news in Kuwait, in English or Arabic. Do not repeat anything in the list above, and do not invent or guess a URL.&#10;&#10;Return a JSON object with exactly one key, &quot;suggestions&quot;: a list of up to 5 objects, each with &quot;name&quot;, &quot;type&quot; (one of News Website, Forum, Blog, Reddit, Twitter, Telegram, Facebook, Medium, Quora, Other), &quot;url&quot;, and &quot;reason&quot;." spiffworkflow:aiResponseSchema="{&quot;type&quot;: &quot;object&quot;, &quot;required&quot;: [&quot;suggestions&quot;], &quot;properties&quot;: {&quot;suggestions&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;array&quot;, &quot;items&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;object&quot;, &quot;required&quot;: [&quot;name&quot;, &quot;type&quot;, &quot;url&quot;, &quot;reason&quot;], &quot;properties&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;string&quot;}, &quot;type&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;string&quot;}, &quot;url&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;string&quot;}, &quot;reason&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;string&quot;}}}}}}">
      <bpmn:documentation>Prompt/provider/model/temperature come from the linked "Threat Source Expander" AI Agent Configuration (already seeded in one_bpmn — see promote_threat_agents_to_bpmn patch, which also strips the config's old str.format-style {source_list} placeholder now that the source list is supplied here as Jinja instead). aiStopOnError=false so a bad LLM response degrades to no suggestions this run rather than failing the whole pipeline, matching the original LangGraph node's try/except behaviour.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>f3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="check_duplicates" name="Check Duplicates" spiffworkflow:serverScript="Threat Discovery — Check Duplicates" spiffworkflow:scriptType="Server Script" spiffworkflow:scriptName="Threat Discovery — Check Duplicates">
      <bpmn:documentation>Drops suggestions whose normalized URL already exists on a Threat Source. Writes extracted_sources. (No reachability check — see the process-level documentation.)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>f4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="generate_keywords" name="AI Agent Task: Generate New Keywords" spiffworkflow:serviceType="ai_agent" spiffworkflow:aiAgentConfig="Threat Keyword Generator" spiffworkflow:aiStopOnError="false" spiffworkflow:aiOutputVariable="keyword_result" spiffworkflow:aiResponseFormat="json" spiffworkflow:aiUserPrompt="Existing active keywords: {{ (active_keywords or []) | map(attribute='keyword') | join(', ') }}&#10;&#10;Suggest 10 NEW related keywords (English and Arabic) that would help discover security threat information in Kuwait — crime, security incidents, public safety, emergencies. Do not repeat anything in the list above.&#10;&#10;Return a JSON object with exactly one key, &quot;keywords&quot;: a list of objects, each with &quot;keyword&quot; and &quot;language&quot; (&quot;English&quot; or &quot;Arabic&quot;)." spiffworkflow:aiResponseSchema="{&quot;type&quot;: &quot;object&quot;, &quot;required&quot;: [&quot;keywords&quot;], &quot;properties&quot;: {&quot;keywords&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;array&quot;, &quot;items&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;object&quot;, &quot;required&quot;: [&quot;keyword&quot;, &quot;language&quot;], &quot;properties&quot;: {&quot;keyword&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;string&quot;}, &quot;language&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;string&quot;}}}}}}">
      <bpmn:documentation>Prompt/provider/model come from the linked "Threat Keyword Generator" AI Agent Configuration, same treatment as the expander above.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>f5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="save_to_erp" name="Save to ERP" spiffworkflow:serverScript="Threat Discovery — Save to ERP" spiffworkflow:scriptType="Server Script" spiffworkflow:scriptName="Threat Discovery — Save to ERP">
      <bpmn:documentation>Terminal write step. Creates Threat Keyword (source_type=AI Generated) for each new keyword not already present, and Threat Source (status=Pending) for each extracted source, then commits — identical output contract to the retired LangGraph pipeline's erp_saver node.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>f6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="end_discovery" name="Discovery Complete">
      <bpmn:incoming>f7</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f1" sourceRef="timer_start" targetRef="load_keywords" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f2" sourceRef="load_keywords" targetRef="load_existing_sources" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f3" sourceRef="load_existing_sources" targetRef="expand_sources" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f4" sourceRef="expand_sources" targetRef="check_duplicates" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f5" sourceRef="check_duplicates" targetRef="generate_keywords" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f6" sourceRef="generate_keywords" targetRef="save_to_erp" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f7" sourceRef="save_to_erp" targetRef="end_discovery" />
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_1">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_1" bpmnElement="threat_source_discovery_process">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="timer_start_di" bpmnElement="timer_start">
        <dc:Bounds x="40" y="202" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="20" y="245" width="76" height="27" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="load_keywords_di" bpmnElement="load_keywords">
        <dc:Bounds x="140" y="180" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="load_existing_sources_di" bpmnElement="load_existing_sources">
        <dc:Bounds x="320" y="180" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="expand_sources_di" bpmnElement="expand_sources">
        <dc:Bounds x="500" y="180" width="140" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="check_duplicates_di" bpmnElement="check_duplicates">
        <dc:Bounds x="720" y="180" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="generate_keywords_di" bpmnElement="generate_keywords">
        <dc:Bounds x="900" y="180" width="140" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="save_to_erp_di" bpmnElement="save_to_erp">
        <dc:Bounds x="1120" y="180" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="end_discovery_di" bpmnElement="end_discovery">
        <dc:Bounds x="1300" y="202" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="1278" y="245" width="80" height="27" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f1_di" bpmnElement="f1">
        <di:waypoint x="76" y="220" />
        <di:waypoint x="140" y="220" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f2_di" bpmnElement="f2">
        <di:waypoint x="240" y="220" />
        <di:waypoint x="320" y="220" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f3_di" bpmnElement="f3">
        <di:waypoint x="420" y="220" />
        <di:waypoint x="500" y="220" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f4_di" bpmnElement="f4">
        <di:waypoint x="640" y="220" />
        <di:waypoint x="720" y="220" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f5_di" bpmnElement="f5">
        <di:waypoint x="820" y="220" />
        <di:waypoint x="900" y="220" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f6_di" bpmnElement="f6">
        <di:waypoint x="1040" y="220" />
        <di:waypoint x="1120" y="220" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f7_di" bpmnElement="f7">
        <di:waypoint x="1220" y="220" />
        <di:waypoint x="1300" y="220" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
